ACCESS TEST: Verified original-PDF access on HKF-093.pdf — physical page 2, section "3.1 System composition", exact 8-word contiguous excerpt: "Edge nodes possess local computing and caching capabilities."
SOURCE & GOVERNANCE STATEMENT: Only HKF-093 was available as an original PDF; all other accessible records were screened from local Apple PDFKit selectable-body extracts (reports-1.txt through reports-8.txt). These are independent AI screening decisions and cannot be represented as human decisions.
WORKER-USE & ACCESS BLOCKER STATEMENT: Eight non-overlapping subagent workers were initially assigned to reports-1.txt through reports-8.txt (17 IDs each: c_1a3244a5f51b7291 HKF-001..HKF-017; c_11e567ba362c46c9 HKF-018..HKF-034; c_492357477f6f4750 HKF-035..HKF-051; c_77f8438886400692 HKF-052..HKF-068; c_d9fb53ae4a0b728f HKF-069..HKF-085; c_4c3f45d2fef106d7 HKF-086..HKF-102; c_480365807750fc6c HKF-103..HKF-119; c_48ceac3e0eb0d8b4 HKF-120..HKF-136), but all 8 failed because subagents do not inherit the parent session's connected local folder access. All screening was therefore executed directly within the parent Task. Because the read tool ignores line-range offsets and truncates each reports-*.txt file at 256,000 characters while shell commands are prohibited by task boundaries, 90 records located beyond the 256,000-character boundary (and the truncated tail pages of HKF-058 and HKF-073) could not be read and are marked AWAITING_CLASSIFICATION.
